      <div class="about-section" id="about-copying">
        <h3>&#x29C9;&#xFE0E; Viewing &amp; Copying</h3>
        <p>Click any entry to fill the display panel at the top with its decrypted fields. The <strong>Username</strong>, <strong>2FA token</strong>, and <strong>Password</strong> rows are <strong>click-to-copy</strong> &mdash; click anywhere on the row to copy that field to the clipboard. A brief flash confirms the copy.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:6px">Each copyable row carries a dimmed <strong>&#x29C9;&#xFE0E; copy glyph</strong> on its right edge that brightens when you hover the row, marking it as copyable at a glance. The glyph is only a visual cue &mdash; the whole row is the click target, so copying works the same on touch screens where there is no hover.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:6px">A copied secret is <strong>auto-cleared from the clipboard after 45 seconds</strong>, and immediately on any lock, so it never lingers there.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:6px"><strong>Custom fields</strong> appear as their own click-to-copy rows; any marked <em>secret</em> show masked (&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;) but still copy on click. If the entry has <strong>password history</strong>, a collapsible <strong>&#x23F1;&#xFE0E; Password history</strong> row lists previously used passwords (each with the date it was replaced, newest 20 kept), also click-to-copy.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:6px">Next to the password, a <strong>&#x1F4DD;&#xFE0E; Modified</strong> column shows the date the password was last changed &mdash; or the creation date, if it never has. Hover it for a tooltip with the entry's <strong>creation date</strong> and <strong>age</strong>. Entries saved before this tracking existed show a best-effort creation date (prefixed &ldquo;&le;&rdquo;) inferred from the oldest password-history entry, or the modified date if there is no history &mdash; both are upper bounds on the true creation time.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="about-section" id="about-shortcuts">
        <h3>&#x2328;&#xFE0E; Keyboard Shortcuts</h3>
        <p>Single-key shortcuts work whenever you are not typing in a field. <kbd>Shift</kbd>&#x202F;<kbd>Enter</kbd> works inside the entry form, and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>&#x202F;<kbd>K</kbd> works from anywhere (even while typing).</p>
